        <h2>What Are Cookies?</h2>
        <p>
          This Cookie Policy applies to
          <strong>Specialised Steering (Pty) Ltd</strong> ("we", "our", or
          "us") and explains how we use cookies on
          <a href="https://www.specialisedsteering.com"
            >specialisedsteering.com</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you load a
          website. They help the site function properly, improve security,
          provide a better user experience, and allow us to analyse performance.
        </p>

        <h2>How We Use Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          We use first-party and third-party cookies. First-party cookies are
          essential for the website to work correctly and do not collect
          personally identifiable data.
        </p>
        <p>
          Third-party cookies help us understand how you interact with the site,
          keep our services secure, and improve your experience on future
          visits.
        </p>

        <h2>Types of Cookies We Use</h2>
        <div class="cky-audit-table-element"></div>

        <h3>First-Party Cookies We Use</h3>
        <p>Our website sets the following first-party cookies:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>A/B Testing (ab_near_me_meta):</strong> Used to provide a
            consistent website experience by remembering which content variation
            you were shown. This cookie helps us optimise our website content
            and user experience. It stores only a single letter (A or B) and
            contains no personally identifiable information. Duration: 90 days.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Specific Third-Party Services We Use</h3>
        <p>Our website uses cookies from the following third-party services:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Analytics:</strong> To analyse website traffic and
            user behaviour
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Tag Manager:</strong> To manage website tags and
            tracking
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google reCAPTCHA:</strong> To protect forms from spam and
            abuse
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>CookieYes:</strong> To manage cookie consent and preferences
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          For more information about our use of third-party services, please see
          our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
